      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "When you see a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "zit",
            "zh": "丘疹"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on your face, you may go to the mirror. So do "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "dolphins",
            "ref": "v-dolphin"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "! They are much wiser than we thought."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Bottle-nosed dolphins can "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "recognize",
            "ref": "v-recognize"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " themselves in a mirror—just like humans!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Presley and Tab are two bottle-nosed dolphins. They live in a pool with "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "reflective",
            "ref": "v-reflective"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " glass walls in the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "New York Aquarium",
            "zh": "纽约水族馆"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "Researchers",
            "ref": "v-researcher"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " found Presley and Tab were able to see their own reflections. Let’s see what they did!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "People made "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "ink",
            "zh": "油墨"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "marks",
            "ref": "v-mark"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on different parts of the dolphins’ bodies every week. Guess what? Every time their bodies were marked, the dolphins made more trips to the mirror than usual."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "If the marks were on their "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "tummies",
            "zh": "肚子"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", they would "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "expose",
            "ref": "v-expose"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " their tummies to the mirror and look at them for a long time."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Where did this come from? Is it still there?” the dolphins might think."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
